course: dictionary
lesson: 2151
title: Coral: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word coral can name a stony material, a tiny sea animal, or a colour. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer wants. Ask yourself: which meaning fits here?
explain: «Parrotfish bite algae off coral with beak-like teeth.» Parrotfish do not bite a colour, and they do not bite a pink paint. They bite the hard, stony material that reefs are made of, so coral means that material here.
explain: «The coral pink dress was in the shop window.» Here coral is a colour, because you can have a pink dress but not a pink animal. Read the words around coral, check your meaning in the sentence, and you will find the right one.
fact: Coral is a hard, stony material made by tiny sea animals over many years.
fact: A coral is one of those tiny animals, or a group of them. Corals are animals, not plants.
fact: Coral pink is a pinkish-orange colour.
fact: «Coral reefs cover less than one percent of the ocean floor but are home to a huge share of sea life.»
fact: «When water gets too warm, corals push out their algae and turn white, which is called bleaching.» The Great Barrier Reef near Australia is the largest coral reef in the world.
exercise: «Parrotfish bite algae off coral with beak-like teeth.» In this sentence, what is coral? | *A hard, stony material built by tiny sea animals | A kind of fish that bites | A pinkish-orange colour | A sandy beach
exercise: «The coral pink dress was in the shop window.» What does coral mean here? | *A pinkish-orange colour | A tiny sea animal | A hard, stony material | A type of seaweed
exercise: «When water gets too warm, corals push out their algae and turn white, which is called bleaching.» Find and copy the word that names what happens when corals turn white. | *bleaching | water | algae | warm
test: «The coral that looks like rocks and plants is really made of tiny animals.» Why is coral not a plant? | Because it grows only in cold water | Because it is a rock from the seabed | *Because it is made of tiny animals | Because it is a pinkish-orange colour
test: «Coral reefs cover less than one percent of the ocean floor but are home to a huge share of sea life.» Which part of this sentence shows that reefs are very important for sea creatures? | Ocean floor | Coral reefs cover | Less than one percent of the ocean floor | *Home to a huge share of sea life
exam: «When water gets too warm, corals push out their algae and turn white.» Why do corals turn white? | They are too cold to stay pink | *They push out the algae that live inside them | They have turned into sand | They are painted white by the sun
